@@ -130 +130,41 @@ unfinished work above. Budget extensions must reflect a real operator request, n
 silent response to an exhausted allowance.
+
+## Authorized HTTP writes and pairing
+
+Start the Hunt with `policy.allow_state_changing_http: true` for an operator-authorized pairing or
+write workflow. Reuse the target's standing authorization; no additional per-call approval is
+introduced. Leave `capabilities: []` to derive the available set. An existing read-only Hunt keeps
+its immutable authority: start a new Hunt with the requested write policy rather than silently
+changing the old one.
+
+`http.request_active` accepts POST, PUT, PATCH and DELETE on web, API, network and device targets.
+For example, after selecting the actual device service from evidence, call
+`POST /hunts/{hunt_id}/capabilities/http.request_active` with:
+
+```json
+{"idempotency_key":"pair-start-001","input":{"method":"PUT","origin":"http://192.168.1.50:7345","path":"/pairing/start","json_body":{"DEVICE_NAME":"ShakerScan"}}}
+```
+
+The address, port, path and body above are illustrative, not a universal TV protocol. Use exactly
+one bounded JSON, form or UTF-8 text body (32 KiB). Selected credentials and sessions retain their
+existing capability grants; never silently widen a read-only profile. Reusable secrets and PINs
+should be supplied through encrypted profiles/collections, not planner body fields. Body values
+are excluded from planner/action summaries; the existing explicitly sensitive HTTP archive remains
+subject to its normal export controls.
+
+`collections.select` can inspect saved write entries without executing them. For a bound
+`confirmed_active` selection, call `collections.replay_active` with the collection ID and returned
+request IDs. The worker replays at most 25 exact saved requests, validates the selection digest,
+and reserves the actual plan's HTTP/state-change budget before traffic. The safe replay operation
+remains GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only.
+
+Both paths retain target pinning, selected credential validation, device health/pacing, durable
+idempotency and measured accounting. A retried identical action key or delivered queue message
+cannot start the same completed write again. Do not use a new key merely because a response was
+lost: inspect the action and target state first. A transport failure does not prove the write had
+no effect. Direct write redirects are returned, not followed automatically. A successful HTTP
+response is an observation, not proof of pairing or a vulnerability.
+
+These capabilities do not implement native WebSocket pairing or vendor-specific challenge/token
+negotiation. The regression fixtures exercise HTTP pairing-shaped requests, not a physical TV or
+a model-to-model evaluation.
